SIFT_V6_FUSE_MAX_ARMS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_BOUNDS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_COLS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_DCOLS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_FCOLS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_FILTERS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_INSETS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_KEYS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_MASKS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_VK_AK_MAX_F	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_VK_DEC_SLOTS	slots of a fixed internal table or shared array: a capacity of the implementation that a full table handles by waiting or falling back, not a limit on a statement
SIFT_VM_DIRTY_MAX_BLOOM_BLOCKS	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
SIFT_WIN_NO_LIMIT	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SORT_LIMIT_GUESS	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
SORT_RESIDUAL_MAX_ROWS	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
VK_MAX_EXTENSION_NAME_SIZE	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
WARN_SLOTS	slots of a fixed internal table or shared array: a capacity of the implementation that a full table handles by waiting or falling back, not a limit on a statement
SIFT_DICTSEEN_MAX_CODES	the codes of a dictionary the distinct-values set of a parallel scan reads as codes: a larger one is read as strings, the rows are the same
SIFT_DICTSEEN_MAX_BYTES	the bytes of a dictionary the distinct-values set of a parallel scan reads as codes: a larger one is read as strings, the rows are the same
SIFT_PAR_RING_MAX_BYTES	memory bound of the chunks of the two-stage parallel strategy: it changes which strategy a plan takes, not its rows
SIFT_PAR_TWO_STAGE_MAX_GROUPS	size of the table a participant of the two-stage parallel strategy keeps before it hands it over (the direct-table bound of the cost model): a speed choice, the rows are the same
SIFT_PAR_WIDE_WORKERS	the number of parallel workers from which the radix strategy uses more partitions: a tuning bound, the rows are the same
V6_NUMERIC_MAX_DIGITS	size of the digit buffer of a 128-bit numeric (the largest value of the format has 12 base-10000 digits): a representation size, not a limit a user reaches
CHAIN_SLOTS	slots of the backend cache of delta chains of a table (table/f2/f2_chain_cache.c): an internal cache bound, the rows the statement reads are the same
OSA_MAX_RUNS	sorted runs an ordered-set aggregate keeps while its scan goes on (agg/osa_runs.c): past it OSA_FANIN of them merge into one and the answer is the same
PART_AUX_SLOTS	slots of the cache of the auxiliary records of the parts a scan reads (col/granule/part_read.c): an internal cache bound with no visible effect
PIN_CX_MAX_BLOCK	largest block of the memory context of the part pins (col/f2/f2_gbuf.c): an internal allocation size
QUAR_CACHE_SLOTS	slots of the memo of the quarantine verdicts of a backend (core/quarantine.c): an internal cache bound with no visible effect
SIFT_F2S_EXCL_SLOTS	the granules whose excluded rows an overlay remembers, the last ones asked for (col/f2/f2_scope_int.h): a cache of one statement, a miss reads them again and the rows are the same
SIFT_HYB_ACL_MAX_KEYS	mirrors SIFT_SEMI_MAX_SET, which has a row in SIFT_LIMITS
SIFT_PACK_MAX_BYTES	bytes of the packed group key of one row (agg/v6/v6_group_fast.h): past it the keys are hashed one by one and the rows are the same
SIFT_PACK_MAX_KEYS	group keys of the packed group key (agg/v6/v6_group_fast.h): past it the keys are hashed one by one and the rows are the same
SIFT_SCOPE_OVERLAY_MAX_PAIR_EDITS	pair edits the journal may name for a scope overlay to serve a read (col/scope_v6/overlay.h): past them the overlay is not opened and the read goes the other way, the rows are the same
SIFT_TOPK_MAX_ITEMS	sort items of the group Top-K of a SiftAggV6 scan (agg/v6/v6_group_topk.h): a statement with more keeps the normal plan and the rows are the same
SIFT_TOPK_MAX_K	LIMIT plus OFFSET of the group Top-K of a SiftAggV6 scan (agg/v6/v6_group_topk.h): a statement above it keeps the normal plan and the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_CASE	arms of a CASE of a derived column of a SiftAggV6 scan (agg/v6/v6.h): a statement with more keeps the normal plan and the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_DERIVE	derived columns of one SiftAggV6 scan (agg/v6/v6.h): a statement with more keeps the normal plan and the rows are the same
SIFT_V6_MAX_TOPK_ITEMS	sort items of the Top-K of a SiftAggV6 scan (agg/v6/v6.h): a statement with more keeps the normal plan and the rows are the same
SNAP_MAX_READS	the cubes of keys a scope snapshot keeps for one statement (col/f2/f2_scope_snap.c), a ring: the oldest read is dropped and a key asked for again is read again, the rows are the same
INV_MAX_BUDGET	the bytes the bm25 build buffer holds before it spills to a run (bm25/inv.c), a performance threshold: the index is the same
ROUTE_MAX_SHARE_PCT	the share of granules above which a scope router is not built (col/f2/f2_scope_route.c), a cost threshold: the rows are the same
SET_INIT_SLOTS	the slots a group set starts with (agg/v6/group.c), it grows by doubling: no result depends on it
CARRY_FIRST_SLOTS	the slots a window carry table starts with (agg/v6/v6_win_carry.c): it grows by doubling, no result depends on it
CMP_MAX_KW	words of a compact group key (agg/v6/v6_group_compact.c): wider keys use the normal group table, the rows are the same
CMP_MAX_WORDS	words of a compact group key (agg/v6/v6_group_cmp.h): wider keys use the normal group table, the rows are the same
MONTH_MAX_DAYS	days of a month a calendar table holds (agg/v6/v6_tseries_fast.c): a fixed calendar fact, not a limit
MONTH_SLOTS	slots of the month table of an unnest group (agg/v6/v6_unnest_run.c): a capacity of the implementation, past it the heap plan runs with the same rows
OUT_SLOTS	slots of the output batch of an unnest group (agg/v6/v6_unnest_run.c): a capacity of the implementation, a full batch is flushed
RG_FIRST_SLOTS	the groups a regrouped window starts with (agg/v6/v6_win_par.c): it grows by doubling, no result depends on it
RG_MAX_GROUPS	groups a regrouped window holds (agg/v6/v6_win_par.c): past it the sorted window runs, the rows are the same
RG_MAX_ROWS	rows a regrouped window holds (agg/v6/v6_win_par.c): past it the sorted window runs, the rows are the same
SEARCH_MAX_ARMS	arms of a search the planner prices (agg/search.c): past it the normal plan runs with the same rows
SEMI_ENTRIES	entries of the semi-join set cache (bm25/semi_cache.c): a cache bound with no visible effect
SIFT_ARITH_MAX_STACK	the stack of a postfix arithmetic expression (agg/v6/v6_plan_rewrite.h): a longer expression is not planned, the rows are the same
SIFT_ARITH_MAX_TOKENS	tokens of a postfix arithmetic expression (agg/v6/v6_plan_rewrite.h): a longer expression is not planned, the rows are the same
SIFT_DICT_MAX_VALUES	values of a dictionary the parallel cost model prices (agg/v6/v6_par_path.c): a cost threshold, the rows are the same
SIFT_LOCK_MAX_K	the top-K a lock-free heap keeps (agg/v6/v6_plan_rewrite.h): a larger K takes the normal path, the rows are the same
SIFT_VN_MAX_FACTORS	factors of an exact numeric product (agg/v6/v6_expr_num.h): a longer product is not planned, the rows are the same
SIFT_WIN_CARRY_MAX_VARS	variables a window carry holds (agg/v6/v6_win_carry.h): past it the plain window runs, the rows are the same
SORT_LOOKUP_MAX_ROWS	rows of a projection sort lookup (agg/v6/v6_proj_sort_plan.c): past it the sort runs, the rows are the same
STAT_SLOTS	slots of the column statistics cache of the planner (agg/v6/v6_colstat.c): a cache bound with no visible effect
SUM_ROW_LIMIT	rows an exact numeric sum folds in one step (agg/v6/v6_expr_num.c): a batch size, the result is the same
UNIQUE_LOCK_SLOTS	the key locks of a unique index (bm25/unique.c): keys that share a slot wait for each other, no result depends on it
